{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tracker search window tuning tracker search window tuning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","fileName":"Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tracker Search Window Tuning","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","Tracking Pattern Search and Anchor Regions","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tracker search window tuning tracker search window tuning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","fileName":"Tracker Search Window Tuning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tracker Search Window Tuning","heading":"Tracker Search Window Tuning","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The search region must be large enough to contain the feature's next-frame motion but not so large that a similar feature elsewhere becomes a tempting match. A tiny pattern may lock onto grain rather than a durable image detail, while an oversized pattern includes changing material that weakens recognition. When a track fails, inspect both the selected feature and its search boundary before assuming the entire shot is untrackable. The pattern, search, and anchor roles are separated in [[Tracking Pattern Search and Anchor Regions]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","Tracking Pattern Search and Anchor Regions","digitalvisualeffe